1. First, list your EC2 instances and their tags
bash

aws ec2 describe-instances --query 'Reservations[*].Instances[*].[InstanceId,Tags]' --output json
2. Check AWS Backup plans that might use tags
bash

# List all backup plans
aws backup list-backup-plans

# Get details of each backup plan (replace PLAN-ID with actual ID)
aws backup get-backup-plan --backup-plan-id PLAN-ID

# Check backup selection resources (which might use tags)
aws backup list-backup-selections --backup-plan-id PLAN-ID
aws backup get-backup-selection --backup-plan-id PLAN-ID --selection-id SELECTION-ID
3. Review IAM policies that reference tags
bash

# List all policies
aws iam list-policies

# Get detailed policy document (look for Condition elements with tags)
aws iam get-policy-version --policy-arn POLICY-ARN --version-id VERSION-ID
4. Check EventBridge (CloudWatch Events) rules
bash

# List all rules
aws events list-rules

# Get rule details to see if tags are used in the pattern
aws events describe-rule --name RULE-NAME
5. Examine Systems Manager Tag-based operations
bash

# List all SSM documents
aws ssm list-documents

# Get document details
aws ssm get-document --name DOCUMENT-NAME
6. Check Lambda functions that might filter by tags
bash

# List Lambda functions
aws lambda list-functions

# Get function code location to review it
aws lambda get-function --function-name FUNCTION-NAME
7. Check cost allocation tags
bash

# List cost allocation tags
aws ce list-cost-allocation-tags
8. Check Data Lifecycle Manager policies (for automated snapshots)
bash

# List DLM policies
aws dlm get-lifecycle-policies

# Get policy details
aws dlm get-lifecycle-policy --policy-id POLICY-ID
9. Check Auto Scaling Groups that might use tags for scaling
bash

# List Auto Scaling Groups
aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups

# Get tags on Auto Scaling Groups
aws autoscaling describe-tags
10. Resource Groups that use tags
bash

# List resource groups
aws resource-groups list-groups

# Get details of each group
aws resource-groups get-group --group-name GROUP-NAME
